{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JsVCMKAkqqoptdRpQX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft this, there's a problem with the main promise and a few things I need from you.\n\n**The \"same cleaner every single time\" promise.** Your new system is a regular cleaner plus a named backup. That means some visits will be done by the backup. And with 7 of 18 cleaners leaving last year, you can't guarantee anyone stays. Cleaner changes were the second most common reason people left, so these readers will notice if the promise breaks. I'd suggest something you can keep, like: \"You'll have your own regular cleaner, plus a named backup you'll meet ahead of time, never a stranger.\" Does that work, or is there something else that would make \"every time\" true?\n\nMy other questions:\n\n1. **Is anything different for cleaners now?** For example, a raise, better hours or less turnover so far this year. If so, I can say \"your cleaner is more likely to stay,\" not just \"we've changed how we assign people.\"\n2. **Does the $99 first cleaning have conditions?** Is there a deadline, or does it require booking every-other-week service after that?\n3. **What does the reader actually get for the extra $25?** Should I name the $140 apps directly, or just say what you do differently (employees, insurance on every visit) without comparing?\n4. **Who signs it, and how do people rebook?** Your name and title, plus a link, phone number or \"reply to this email.\""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":564,"cache_read_input_tokens":9533,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":564},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i