{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JtTyiLvqJJrpbT591e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't name any app companies. Naming them would invite a comparison and wouldn't make your case stronger.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own cleaner, and $99 to come back\n\nHi [First name],\n\nWhen customers left us last year, the reasons we heard most were price and a different cleaner showing up too often. We've worked on both.\n\nSince July, every customer has their own regular cleaner, plus a named backup for sick days and holidays. You'll always know who's coming. Since then, only 1 of our 18 cleaners has left.\n\nWe'll be straight about price. An every-other-week cleaning for a 3-bedroom home is $165 with us. App services nearby charge about $140. The difference pays for cleaners who are our employees, earning $21 an hour, with insurance on every visit. Most app services use contractors with no insurance on the visit.\n\nCome back before December 31 and your first cleaning is $99. There's no contract, and you can cancel any time.\n\nReply to this email or call 555-0164 to book.\n\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nA few notes:\n\n- **The backup.** Earlier I suggested saying customers would meet their backup ahead of time. I left that out because you didn't tell me it happens. If it does, adding \"you'll meet your backup in advance\" would make the email stronger.\n- **The 3-bedroom price.** If you have customers with smaller or larger homes, consider adding \"for example\" before the price so it doesn't read as their quote.\n- **The cleaner numbers.** \"Only 1 of 18 since July\" is true, but it covers just four months. Keep using that line only while it stays true."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":10097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral